## Approach

- Create a new array to store the elements from both sorted arrays.
- Use two pointers to compare the elements of both arrays.
- Add the smaller element to the result array and move its pointer.
- Add the remaining elements after one array is completely traversed.
- Find the middle element of the merged array.
- If the length is even, take the average of the two middle elements.
- Otherwise, return the middle element as the median.
